{
  "id": "P048",
  "slug": "mini-csv-parser-with-quotes",
  "title": "Stateful Quoted CSV Parser",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": [
    "strings",
    "parsing"
  ],
  "estimatedMinutes": 22,
  "relatedModules": [
    "a3-strings-io",
    "a9-files-csv-json"
  ],
  "entry": {
    "type": "function",
    "name": "parse_csv"
  },
  "compare": "exact",
  "tests": {
    "visible": [
      {
        "label": "Quoted fields with commas and escaped double quotes",
        "args": [
          "id,note\n1,\"Hello, world\"\n2,\"Said \"\"OK\"\" twice\"\n"
        ],
        "expected": [
          [
            "id",
            "note"
          ],
          [
            "1",
            "Hello, world"
          ],
          [
            "2",
            "Said \"OK\" twice"
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Empty text yields empty rows list",
        "args": [
          ""
        ],
        "expected": []
      }
    ],
    "hidden": [
      {
        "label": "Empty quoted fields and trailing comma",
        "args": [
          "a,\"\","
        ],
        "expected": [
          [
            "a",
            "",
            ""
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Quoted newline inside a cell",
        "args": [
          "k,v\n1,\"line1\nline2\"\n"
        ],
        "expected": [
          [
            "k",
            "v"
          ],
          [
            "1",
            "line1\nline2"
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "CRLF line endings normalized",
        "args": [
          "x,y\r\n3,4\r\n"
        ],
        "expected": [
          [
            "x",
            "y"
          ],
          [
            "3",
            "4"
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "No trailing newline on final row",
        "args": [
          "h1,h2\n10,20"
        ],
        "expected": [
          [
            "h1",
            "h2"
          ],
          [
            "10",
            "20"
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Escaped quotes at start and end of field",
        "args": [
          "\"\"\"hi\"\"\",end"
        ],
        "expected": [
          [
            "\"hi\"",
            "end"
          ]
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "hints": [
    "Use a character-by-character state machine rather than line.split(\",\") because quoted fields can contain BOTH commas and embedded newlines!",
    "Track `in_quotes = False`. While `in_quotes`, if `text[i:i+2] == '\"\"'`, append `\"` and advance `i += 2`; if single `\"`, flip `in_quotes = False`. Outside quotes, `,` finishes a cell and `\\n` finishes a row.",
    "Pseudocode:\n  walk i with while i < len(text):\n      if in_quotes: handle \"\" -> \" vs closing \"\n      else: handle \", comma, \\r\\n or \\n, or ordinary char\n  flush trailing cell/row if non-empty"
  ],
  "sources": [
    "python-tutorial",
    "python-stdtypes-docs"
  ]
}
